{"chapter": "sheaves", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "009Z", "placeholders": {}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:4b6d43a14a272e811b0983bc38454799a0ceeb28f876c99b97ba8cd91b3e210c", "source_text": "Omitted.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:872a8cfa74892c6e6464bd864d9f1c292f4f523caba3e51ac3dafbfc84db48f6", "unit_id": "tag:00A7:proof"}
{"chapter": "sheaves", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "009Z", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$j_*$", "MATH_0002": "$j_!$", "MATH_0003": "$U$", "MATH_0004": "$X$", "MATH_0005": "$j_!$", "STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:7df10b4bbbb6754119ea4d0df8bc6710ca2599831bf1a91fc45e03155f280451", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:ffc2bd0698f8a3f7da40bcb13ee3dfe72c89128e97a70479aaa50a65d003608d", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nNote that by the lemmas above, both the functors\n<MATH_0001> and <MATH_0002> are fully faithful embeddings of\nthe category of sheaves on <MATH_0003> into the category\nof sheaves on <MATH_0004>. It is only true for the functor\n<MATH_0005> that one can easily describe the essential\nimage of this functor.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:643649671386daf3718c946e229117d338c9402189dcce2f88a2ec378bf2e990", "unit_id": "tag:009Z:prose-0005"}
{"chapter": "sheaves", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "009Z", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$X$", "MATH_0002": "$j : U \\to X$", "MATH_0003": "$$\nj_! : \\Sh(U) \\longrightarrow \\Sh(X)\n$$", "MATH_0004": "$\\mathcal{G}$", "MATH_0005": "$\\mathcal{G}_x = \\emptyset$", "MATH_0006": "$x \\in X \\setminus U$"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-equivalence-categories-open}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:67d23042e4472b55e7d8a1b7141028fa21f9de3408cbf0cb5045452ec00c2893", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:30c742ba955a68ad94bb646a3e74e99eee221f3b0abb9f308aa67674ea771e50", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a topological space.\nLet <MATH_0002> be the inclusion of an open subset.\nThe functor\n<MATH_0003>\nis fully faithful. Its essential image consists exactly\nof those sheaves <MATH_0004> such that\n<MATH_0005> for all <MATH_0006>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:efd2eb7cc00d6d10fd7eae20e9c630b7bb3aa482dc7e7031ad8164dd4bc5c108", "unit_id": "tag:00A8:statement"}
{"chapter": "sheaves", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "009Z", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$j^{-1} j_! = \\text{id}$", "MATH_0002": "$\\mathcal{G}$", "MATH_0003": "$$\nj_! j^{-1} \\mathcal{G} \\to \\mathcal{G}\n$$"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:2ae8ec9cc6fc78fcbf6c2a52c3a4efe579d780444bca7838521dcc146d776cbd", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:0cd0f1d173275c7c0947f5e90db146f58010992f79c06c6c4ad87c4a15d3cd20", "source_text": "Fully faithfulness follows formally from <MATH_0001>.\nWe have seen that any sheaf in the image of the functor has\nthe property on the stalks mentioned in the lemma. Conversely, suppose\nthat <MATH_0002> has the indicated property.\nThen it is easy to check that\n<MATH_0003>\nis an isomorphism on all stalks and hence an isomorphism.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:22abbc6c0e11445159a754a2135a46ace76100585a889b54e583902471280b19", "unit_id": "tag:00A8:proof"}
